  :adr/first-live-code-banking-dependency-6493 "the FIRST cloud-itonami-isic-* actor in this fleet to depend on a :banking-family capability library (kotoba-lang/swift, kotoba-lang/banking's kotoba.banking.api, kotoba-lang/ekyc's kotoba.ekyc) as LIVE CODE rather than cite it in a docstring -- every prior sibling (e.g. ADR-2607080200/6491) explicitly kept the capability lib 'cited but not directly required, self-contained like every prior sibling'. Per explicit owner instruction."
  :adr/ekyc-integration-6493 "a new HARD, un-overridable governor check (factoring.governor/ekyc-verification-invalid-violations, checked at :receivable/verify AND :advance/fund) independently constructs real kotoba.ekyc/verification records for the CLIENT and the ACCOUNT DEBTOR from receivable ground truth and runs kotoba.ekyc/validate against the real JPN 犯収法施行規則 Art.6(1) method catalog. The violation carries the FULL structured result (:ekyc/disposition :ekyc/reasons), a real specific rejection reason, not an abstract boolean -- the first HARD check in this fleet to do so"
  :adr/settlement-instruction-integration-6493 ":advance/fund (actuation 1) and :reserve/settle (actuation 2) now construct a REAL settlement-instruction artifact on every clean commit -- a genuine SWIFT MT103 wire string (kotoba.swift) or a genuine Berlin Group XS2A payment-initiation JSON payload (kotoba.banking.api). CHOSEN: XS2A as the default rail (factoring's actual pattern is the factor's own bank paying its own client, structurally an XS2A payment-initiation, not a correspondent-banking interbank wire); MT103 auto-selected whenever the currency's decimal convention isn't 2 (kotoba.banking.api's own documented limitation -- its amountValue conversion assumes 2 minor units always, so JPY through XS2A would misconvert by 100x) -- a correctness guard, not a preference, that also happens to line up with Japan having no IBAN scheme at all (cited honestly as a coincidence, not the stated rationale). Artifact stored in the audit ledger AND returned in the HTTP response"
  :adr/graceful-degradation-6493 "build-settlement-instruction catches incomplete/invalid banking-detail errors and surfaces a clear :settlement/error marker rather than crashing the commit -- a data-completeness concern, not a governance one; the actuation DECISION (commit/hold per factoring.governor's HARD checks) is unaffected either way"
  :adr/second-json-coercion-bug-fixed-proactively-6493 "ADR-2607142000 found a JSON-string-vs-Clojure-keyword coercion bug live for :debtor-risk-tier (js->clj :keywordize-keys true only keywordizes map KEYS not values). The SAME bug class for the new eKYC fields (:client-ekyc-method etc., and evidence items' own :kind/:fields-confirmed) was found and fixed PROACTIVELY this time, before shipping -- not rediscovered live a second time"
  :adr/live-re-smoke-test-6493 "a JPY receivable run through the full lifecycle against https://factoring.murakumo.cloud before landing: POST /verify response confirmed to carry a real kotoba.ekyc/validate result (disposition=pass); POST /advance and POST /settle responses confirmed to carry a genuine, well-formed SWIFT MT103 wire string with correct value-date/currency/amount; a second case confirmed an unrecognized eKYC method produces a real specific 409 (rule=ekyc-verification-invalid, disposition=fail, reasons=[unrecognized-method]). Test data deleted from the live KV afterward"
  :adr/honesty-boundary-6493 "restated, sharper, now that real artifacts are in play: the ARTIFACTS this actor produces (SWIFT MT103 wire, XS2A JSON payload, eKYC validation) are themselves REAL and spec-conformant, but EVERY one is constructed, ledgered, and returned in the API response, and NEVER transmitted anywhere -- no real SWIFTNet connection, no real bank API call, no real eKYC vendor call. Documented verbatim in worker/README.md, the repo's docs/adr/0003, and this superproject ADR -- three places, because 'deployed and live' is exactly where this boundary is easiest to blur"
  :adr/test-status-6493 "100 tests / 389 assertions repo-wide (82/336 core actor + 18/53 worker HTTP-API), lint-clean"
  :adr/live-url "https://factoring.murakumo.cloud"
